000100 REM depending on a package (install it first: ./mpm install left-malaise)
      * IMPORT is resolved and spliced at load time. resolution order:
      * ./  then $MALAISEPATH  then ./malaise_modules  then a path on a laptop.
       IMPORT "left-malaise"
       PRINT "left-malaise version:"
       PRINT $pkgver
      * the standard library has no string padding, so we borrow the package's
      * routine: set the inputs, GOSUB, read the output back out of the same
      * global variable (there are no parameters and no locals).
       $padstr = "Ada"                         ;
       $padwid = 8                             ;
       GOSUB lpad
       PRINT $padstr
       PRINT LEN $padstr
      * importing it again does nothing (imports are idempotent; nothing else is)
       IMPORT "left-malaise"
       GOTO fin
      *
fin    REM
       FREE($pkgver)
       FREE($padstr)
       FREE($padwid)
